# ATS Resume Checker

Upload a resume (PDF, DOCX or TXT) and get an ATS score out of 100, a score
breakdown, prioritised improvements, keyword gaps and rewritten bullet points.
Optionally paste a job description to score the resume against that job.

Built with [Streamlit](https://streamlit.io) and the Google Gemini API
(Flash model).

## Features

- Reads PDF, DOCX and TXT resumes (up to 5 MB)
- Overall ATS score plus per-category scores
- Prioritised improvements (high, medium, low) with specific fixes
- Found and missing keywords
- Bullet-point rewrites (with placeholders like `[X%]` so nothing is invented)
- Rule-based checks: email, phone, section headings, length
- Optional job description matching
- Downloadable Markdown report

## How the score works

1. Gemini rates the resume from 0 to 100 in each category, following a fixed rubric.
2. The app blends the model's formatting rating with its own rule-based checks
   (contact details, section headings, length), because the model only sees
   extracted text and cannot see the page layout.
3. The final score is a weighted average calculated in code, not by the model.

| Category | Without job description | With job description |
|---|---|---|
| Job description match | n/a | 30% |
| Keywords and skills | 25% | 15% |
| Achievements and impact | 25% | 20% |
| Sections and structure | 20% | 15% |
| ATS-friendly formatting | 15% | 10% |
| Clarity and grammar | 15% | 10% |

> This is an estimate. Real ATS products (Workday, Greenhouse, Lever and others)
> each parse resumes differently, and no tool can reproduce their exact scores.
> Use the result as guidance on what to fix, not as a guarantee.

## Run locally

Requires Python 3.10 or newer.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/ats-resume-checker.git
cd ats-resume-checker

python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate        # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

pip install -r requirements.txt
streamlit run app.py
```

### Add your Gemini API key

Get a free key from [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/apikey), then
use any one of these:

- Paste it in the sidebar when the app runs (easiest, nothing is stored).
- Create `.streamlit/secrets.toml` in the project folder:

  ```toml
  GEMINI_API_KEY = "your-key-here"
  ```

- Or set an environment variable: `export GEMINI_API_KEY="your-key-here"`

### Choose a different model

Gemini model names change over time. The default is `gemini-3.5-flash`. If it is
unavailable for your key, the app automatically tries `gemini-2.5-flash`. To use
another model, edit the "Gemini model" box in the sidebar, or add this to your
secrets:

```toml
GEMINI_MODEL = "gemini-2.5-flash"
```

See the current list at <https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models>.

## Deploy on Streamlit Community Cloud

1. Push this project to a GitHub repository (the repository can be public or private).
2. Go to <https://share.streamlit.io> and sign in with GitHub.
3. Click **Create app**, choose your repository and branch, and set the main file
   path to `app.py`.
4. Open **Advanced settings** and paste your secrets:

   ```toml
   GEMINI_API_KEY = "your-key-here"
   ```

5. Click **Deploy**. The first build takes a few minutes.

Never commit `.streamlit/secrets.toml` or any API key to GitHub.

## Project structure

```
ats-resume-checker/
├── app.py            # the whole app
├── requirements.txt  # Python dependencies
├── README.md
└── .gitignore        # keeps secrets and virtualenvs out of Git
```

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
|---|---|
| "Almost no text could be read" | The PDF is a scan or image. Export a text-based PDF or use DOCX. |
| "Gemini rejected the API key" | Check the key and that the Gemini API is enabled for it. |
| "Rate limit or quota reached" | Wait a minute, or check your quota in Google AI Studio. |
| "That model is not available" | Change the model name in the sidebar, e.g. `gemini-2.5-flash`. |
| Scores differ slightly between runs | Normal for AI output. Rule-based checks stay identical. |

## Privacy

The text of the uploaded resume (and job description, if given) is sent to the
Google Gemini API to be analysed. The app does not store files or results on
disk. Review Google's API data policy before using real resumes of other people.

## Limitations

- Scanned or image-only resumes cannot be read.
- Text inside images, headers, footers and text boxes may be missed, which is
  also what happens in many real ATS systems.
- Very long resumes are truncated to the first 20,000 characters.
